  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason includes: (1) the maximum outcomes (6000 vs. 3000), and (2) the probabilities (0.1% vs. 0.2%), which the reason deems negligible. The individual explicitly acknowledges that the probabilities are so low that the difference between them is irrelevant ('derart gering... dass ich dann auch gleich die 6k nehmen kann'), which aligns with the reason's assumption of negligible probability differences. The individual's justification centers on preferring the higher maximum outcome (6000 Euros) when the probability of winning is so low that it doesn't matter which one they choose. This matches the decision reason's rule: prefer the lottery with the more favorable maximum outcome when probability differences are negligible. Therefore, the individual's deliberation process matches both the information considered and the rule of the decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 100
